Bundled assets keep the status recorded for each of them. None is under a licence
that forbids redistribution. Third-party assets are CC0 1.0. AI-generated assets
are owned output under their generator's terms, and they are distributed under
this repository's licence. The records:

- clients/3d-spike/ASSETS.md
    the 3D client's third-party files (Poly Haven, CharMorph, Quaternius; all CC0),
    the Meshy character and the gpt-image-1 garment source art
- presentation/mineworld-default/LICENSES/
    per-asset licence records (Meshy route D+ character, OwlishMedia hair alphas)
- presentation/mineworld-default/2D/references/PROVENANCE.md
  presentation/mineworld-default/3D/references/PROVENANCE.md
    the reference images, generated with ChatGPT, and the crops derived from them
- presentation/mineworld-default/2D/candidates/*.provenance.yaml
    one record per generated 2D candidate
- docs/DECISIONS.md, DEP-8
    the asset-sourcing rules, and the vendor terms that AI-generated assets rest on
    (OpenAI and Meshy), quoted with URLs and the dates they were read

AI-generated content: the reference images, the generated 2D candidates, the
garment source art and the Meshy character were produced with generative models
(OpenAI image models, Meshy image-to-3D) and curated by a person. They are not
human-made artwork, and they should not be presented as such.
